---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.18.0
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - base
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lint_command
defaults:
  qa_task_id: ""
  sanity_task_id: ""
  dev_task_id: ""
  pr_number: ""
  commit: ""
  branch: ""
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
{% set task_id = sanity_task_id if sanity_task_id else task_id %}
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: each numbered deliverable is written; lint passes. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <layer-prs><![CDATA[{{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer-prs>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>
  <workflow>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[If it prints `false`, the bead is not ready: do not claim it or start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Then refuse; never wait: close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, `bead_state` `open`, `reason_md` naming the bead, why it is not ready, which bead or agent must move, and, for a blocker not yet its dependency, the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`, so `bd ready` lists the bead only once the blocker closes. The task assigner re-assigns it then.]]></step>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before any claim, run `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`; when it prints `false` follow a1. The only pre-link checks are frozen PASS history and pinned commit. Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py sanity --bead {{ task_id }} --commit {{ commit }} --worktree {{ worktree_path }}. An unlinked PR is normal: linking happens after the selected sanity PASS. On READY, claim with bd update {{ task_id }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY", then atm task start {{ task_id }} "Check each numbered deliverable".]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once, with `--layer-pr <n>` for each PR in `<layer-prs>` (empty: the single range from `<base>`), and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Keep both raw result arrays; a JEV reply's `data.jev` comes only from `wrap_jev_receipt.py`. When a reviewer's last reply or timeout envelope arrives, record its completion epoch before merging or waiting for shared lint, then merge it immediately with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Append no history until selected merge sets the final verdict. Build one strict selection array, one entry per deliverable; record the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; it ignores stdin. Append history in exact order `sanity-llm`, then `sanity-jev`, both rows with the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run, use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Retain the selected vars as review evidence; do not replace or rewrite the lead-supplied shared hook vars with this narrower report payload. Exit 4: wait for shared lint; retries reuse supplied epochs. Selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[After the selected merge, run .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/atm-task-close.py --role sanity --vars <shared-vars.json>. For PASS, first obtain the sanity-stack result as the coordinator specifies. For FAIL, retain exactly the selected undone deliverable numbers and verbatim reasons; the hook sends sanity-fail on the dev's open task and creates no finding bead. For CANNOT_RUN, the hook refuses this sanity task and leaves its bead open and unassigned. On err, fix the named cause and rerun the hook with the same shared vars. Never close a completed sanity task or bead by hand.]]></step>
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or the work needs an unlanded fix, stop; never stay active waiting. Record BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why> in the CANNOT_RUN report, naming the blocker and any missing edge bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>. Run the hook with verdict CANNOT_RUN; it returns the bead open and unassigned and refuses the task.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the hook closes this task, read ATM again. The console runs tabs replace the chat status table.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
